{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2140-02-17 20:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee, one of the hospitalists. I understand you've been having a hoarse voice for a few days?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2140-02-17 20:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it started about three days ago. It’s been getting worse, and now I can barely speak above a whisper."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2140-02-17 20:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Any trouble breathing, stridor, or chest tightness?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2140-02-17 20:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I’m not having trouble breathing. Just the hoarseness. I did feel a little sick to my stomach that morning with loose stools, but that’s gone now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2140-02-17 20:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. I also see you were recently seen by your laryngologist for vocal cord issues. Can you tell me about that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2140-02-17 20:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, Dr. Patel diagnosed me with paradoxical vocal fold motion disorder. I have scarring and swelling on one of my vocal cords. He wanted me to have a bronchoscopy soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2140-02-17 20:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s right. And you had an appointment scheduled for today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2140-02-17 20:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, at 1 PM. But my voice got so bad last night, I came to the ER instead."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2140-02-17 20:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Understandable. We did a neck X-ray, and there’s no sign of airway blockage or swelling. Your oxygen levels are good, and you’re not in distress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2140-02-17 20:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. Could the cleaning products my daughter used have made it worse?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2140-02-17 20:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. Chemical irritants can aggravate vocal cord inflammation, especially with your existing condition. Smoking can also make it worse—have you been smoking?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2140-02-17 20:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know I should stop… but yes, I still smoke occasionally."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2140-02-17 20:37:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. It’s tough, but quitting would really help your vocal cords and overall health. For now, we’ll continue your omeprazole for reflux, which can also irritate the voice."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2140-02-17 20:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We also gave you albuterol and ipratropium in the ER, which helped a bit. We’ll keep that available if you need it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2140-02-17 20:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. What about my other medications? My blood pressure has been a little high lately."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2140-02-17 20:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your blood pressure is around 142/84, which is better than last admission. We’re increasing your enalapril from 5 to 10 mg daily to help control it, especially since you have hyperaldosteronism."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2140-02-17 20:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my diabetes and headaches? I haven’t had a migraine lately."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2140-02-17 20:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood sugar is stable, so we’re continuing glyburide. No headaches today, which is good. We’re keeping your topiramate and propranolol for prevention."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2140-02-17 20:43:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One lab note: you have a mild metabolic acidosis, likely from your acetazolamide for pseudotumor cerebri. We’ll continue it for now, but your neurologist may adjust it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2140-02-17 20:44:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. So am I going to be here long?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2140-02-17 20:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Actually, your laryngologist was consulted, and he thinks you’re stable to go home. You’re scheduled to see him today at 1 PM for your bronchoscopy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2140-02-17 20:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, I didn’t know they’d reschedule it for today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2140-02-17 20:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, they’ll evaluate for any fixed airway narrowing. In the meantime, we’re sending you home with an inhaler and updated meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2140-02-18 11:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs are stable, and you’re still breathing well. We’re clearing you for discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2140-02-18 11:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. What changes should I watch for?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2140-02-18 11:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call your doctor or come back if you develop breathing trouble, fever, chest pain, or if you can’t keep fluids down. Otherwise, keep your appointment with Dr. Patel."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2140-02-18 11:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my medications—anything changed?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2140-02-18 11:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Enalapril is now 10 mg daily. Glyburide is increased to 5 mg. Everything else stays the same. And please consider the smoking cessation program—we can help you get started."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2140-02-17 20:21:00",
    "admission_end": "2140-02-18 12:45:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of paradoxical vocal fold motion disorder, hypertension due to primary hyperaldosteronism, type 2 diabetes, pseudotumor cerebri, and tobacco use was admitted for worsening dysphonia over three days, likely exacerbated by household chemical exposure and ongoing smoking. She had no airway compromise or respiratory distress. A neck X-ray showed no obstruction, and her oxygenation remained stable. She was managed conservatively with continued omeprazole for laryngeal reflux and as-needed bronchodilators. Her enalapril was increased to 10 mg daily for improved blood pressure control, and glyburide was doubled to 5 mg daily. She was cleared by her laryngologist for discharge with a same-day outpatient bronchoscopy planned to evaluate for subglottic stenosis. She was discharged home in stable condition with medication adjustments and follow-up instructions.",
    "problems": [
      "Other diseases of vocal cords",
      "Dysphonia",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Hyperaldosteronism, unspecified",
      "Other and unspecified hyperlipidemia",
      "Diabetes mellitus without mention of complication, type II or unspecified type, not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Benign intracranial hypertension",
      "Migraine, unspecified, without mention of intractable migraine without mention of status migrainosus",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Tobacco use disorder",
      "Obesity, unspecified",
      "Obstructive sleep apnea (adult)(pediatric)",
      "Long-term (current) use of aspirin"
    ]
  }
}
